* Supplemental REVERSE-POLARITY MIRROR LADDER (twin of gf180-comparator#158/#166)
* Declared by tb.json's `reverse_ladder` key and appended by the harness to
* the SAME transient as the forward bench (one more .include; the fragment's
* `.meas` cards are tb.json reverse_ladder.analyses).
*
* DELIBERATELY A SEPARATE FRAGMENT, NOT MORE OF tb_regeneration.spice AND
* NOT MORE `analyses`: those are consumed fields (pinned by hash by the
* layout/pex tooling, and committed evidence is re-graded from them), so a
* mirrored instance there or an appended `analyses` card would change what
* committed evidence is said to have run. Supplemental characterization only:
* nothing scored reads these quantities.
*
* Instances RA/RB/RC are A/B/C with the stimulus sign MIRRORED: POSITIVE for
* the first strobe, NEGATIVE for the second, so the timed second decision
* actively pulls DOWN an output the first strobe established HIGH. Same
* rungs, same clock, same t_flip, same supply-normalized 0.5 threshold, and
* the manifest times them with `targ ... fall=1 td=35n` -- the same
* second-strobe window as A/B/C, so neither the power-up resolution nor the
* first (positive) decision can be picked up. The dv_*/t_flip parameters are
* defined by the forward fragment (tb_regeneration.spice); this one only
* consumes them. The mirrored instances share the main `vdd` rail (ideal
* source), so instance A's separately integrated supply charge is unaffected.
vsra  sra 0 pwl(0 {dv_big} {t_flip} {dv_big} {t_flip+1n} {-dv_big})
Eapra apra cm sra 0 0.5
Eanra anra cm sra 0 -0.5
ibra  vdd ibnra dc {dut_ib}
Xra   apra anra clk ibnra doutra doutbra vdd 0 comparator_dut

vsrb  srb 0 pwl(0 {dv_mid} {t_flip} {dv_mid} {t_flip+1n} {-dv_mid})
Eaprb aprb cm srb 0 0.5
Eanrb anrb cm srb 0 -0.5
ibrb  vdd ibnrb dc {dut_ib}
Xrb   aprb anrb clk ibnrb doutrb doutbrb vdd 0 comparator_dut

vsrc  src 0 pwl(0 {dv_tiny} {t_flip} {dv_tiny} {t_flip+1n} {-dv_tiny})
Eaprc aprc cm src 0 0.5
Eanrc anrc cm src 0 -0.5
ibrc  vdd ibnrc dc {dut_ib}
Xrc   aprc anrc clk ibnrc doutrc doutbrc vdd 0 comparator_dut

* ---- supply-normalized probes (mirrored outputs) -----------------------
Bdran dran 0 v = 'v(doutra)/v(vdd)'
Bdrbn drbn 0 v = 'v(doutrb)/v(vdd)'
Bdrcn drcn 0 v = 'v(doutrc)/v(vdd)'
